@vsm 1.0
// program_intel_canonical.spec.vsm
// Author: Claude (S3-S5 role, this session on Sonnet 5) + rmw3 (S5), 2026-07-26.
// Closes the loop dispatched by inbox/from_O_program_intel_canonical.vsm (bbh-lab,
// 2026-07-24, authorized rmw3/S5): "[O] commitea el spec program_intel_canonical a canon
// cuando el gate_calibracion pase." The gate passed 2026-07-25T02:48:34Z (commit d5bcad2 on
// bbh-lab). Nobody committed the canon spec for ~24h — this closes that gap. Same pattern as
// the algedonic dossier (docs/rubric/q16_*): delivered work sitting unadjudicated until someone
// reads the live evidence instead of the narrative. Extends finding_validation_gate.spec.vsm
// (this spec's restrictions.json is the missing data source for that gate's unimplemented
// policy/method-compliance condition).

spec(PROGRAM-INTEL-CANONICAL) {

  decision: "RoE/policy + the full H1 program page are PUBLIC — no auth, no 2FA. Proven live
      2026-07-24 (rmw3 read Stripe's Terms unauthenticated) and reconfirmed by this capture
      batch working end-to-end without any session cookie. The prior design ('C2 produces,
      bbh-lab ingests') is RETIRED. bbh-lab OWNS program-intel canonical capture directly via
      its own playwright, keyed on the H1 handle. Directive: inbox/from_O_program_intel_canonical.vsm.",

  // ── WHAT WAS BUILT (verified live on bbh-lab, LXC 111, 2026-07-26) ──────────
  built: {
    parser: "scripts/bbh_guidelines_fetcher.py (+750 lines, commit d5bcad2) — renders a
        program's public H1 page via Playwright, extracts policy text into restrictions.json +
        program_intel.json. Supporting tools landed same session (commit 6b4af1f, rmw3/S5
        approved): bbh_onboard_target.py (target-sheet + canonical-intel integration),
        bbh_target_sheet.py (CSV+ROE -> restrictions.json v3, manual-input path),
        bbh_session_bridge.py (VSM bridge to C2), bbh_state_journal.py, bbh_vsm_update.py,
        import_stripe_scopes.py.",

    gate_calibracion: "PASS. Per the directive's own precondition ('solo si tu captura
        automatica REPRODUCE la verdad humana, seguis'): Stripe was rendered live, diffed
        against inbox/stripe_restrictions.groundtruth.json (the text rmw3 personally verified
        unauthenticated), 5 bugs fixed during calibration, then end-to-end gate (render ->
        parse -> diff vs ground truth) PASSED. Verified live: the resulting restrictions.json
        (targets/stripe/scope/restrictions.json, captured_at 2026-07-25T00:25:20Z) contains
        real extracted content — 7 prohibited_methods, account_requirements with the
        X-Bug-Bounty header + wearehackerone.com alias convention, full pii_handling and
        disclosure_rules prose, not placeholder text.",

    replicated: "Same batch (00:25-00:29Z, 2026-07-25), all 5 currently-tracked real targets
        now have restrictions.json + program_intel.json: stripe (7 prohibited_methods, Gold
        Safe Harbor), gitlab (24.7KB, 9 prohibited_methods, AI-vuln policy), affirm
        (sandbox-only scope, test_accounts_only, test credit cards), matomo (closed scope, 3K
        critical threshold), airtable (staging-only, 0K RCE bounty, enterprise scope). A
        stripe restrictions_v4.json also exists (captured_at 2026-07-24T23:32:00Z,
        scope_assets_count=55, scope_in_scope_count=52, scope_oos_count=3) with a richer
        schema (_capture_method, gated_status, gated_sections, capture_notes) — a second,
        more detailed pass beyond v3; not yet propagated to the other 4 targets.",

    data_integrity_rule: "prohibited_methods=0 with RoE content present must be marked
        prohibited_methods_status: unparsed, never read as permissive-by-default. Not
        independently re-verified in this pass — carried forward from
        project_bbh_mining_strategy as a requirement on any future parser run; check it holds
        the next time this pipeline touches a 6th target.",
  },

  // ── WHAT IS STILL OPEN (verified absent, 2026-07-26 — grep, not assumption) ─
  open: {
    runtime_gate: "NO code reads prohibited_methods to block a tool before it runs. restrictions.json
        exists and is correct; nothing consumes it yet. `grep -rl prohibited_methods scripts/*.py`
        on bbh-lab returns zero hits outside the parser's own output. This is the
        check_policy(tool, target) function named in inbox/from_O_roe_capture.vsm line 25 and
        in finding_validation_gate.spec.vsm's implied 4th condition — designed, not built.
        Scope checking today is asset-level only (bbh_scope_check.py); method-level is manual,
        left to the operator.",

    verify_stage: "The gate_calibracion diff-vs-ground-truth is a real, working check, but it
        is a ONE-TIME calibration against a single hand-verified fixture (Stripe), not the
        'diverse independent verifier LM, re-run per capture' architecture from
        project_bbh_mining_strategy. If the parser is later pointed at a 6th program with
        materially different RoE wording, there is currently no automatic check that its
        extraction is correct — only human review.",

    corpus_expansion: "The delivery commit names its own limitation: 'parser es conservador —
        programas con redaccion distinta a Stripe requieren expansion de
        _KNOWN_PROHIBITED_METHODS (proxima carga corpus-first)'. gitlab/affirm/matomo/airtable
        already went through it once, so their restrictions.json should be spot-checked against
        their actual program pages before being trusted at the same confidence as Stripe's
        ground-truth-calibrated extraction.",

    mining_pipeline: "OpportunityScore (U^beta S^alpha T^tau) ranking of the 590 cached H1
        programs (tools/h1-brain/h1_data.db, count independently verified) has never run.
        `grep -rl OpportunityScore\\|opportunity_score\\|coarse_rank` on bbh-lab returns
        nothing. Target selection remains manual/intuitive — this is unrelated to the
        restrictions.json work above but was asked in the same status pass and is worth
        recording here so it isn't re-asked cold: the 590-program dataset exists, the scoring
        code does not.",
  },

  gate_dependency: "finding_validation_gate.spec.vsm's check_1_scope currently checks two
      things: asset in-scope, vuln class in-scope. project_bbh_mining_strategy already decided
      the gate should be 4 conditions (+ eligible_for_submission, + policy/method-compliance) —
      that decision predates this spec but was never back-ported into
      finding_validation_gate.spec.vsm's text. The restrictions.json this spec ratifies is
      exactly the missing data source for the policy/method-compliance condition. Flagged, not
      fixed here — updating that spec's check list is a small follow-on, separate from closing
      this delivery.",

  process_note: "This delivery sat ~24h between gate_calibracion PASS (2026-07-25T02:48Z) and
      this spec (2026-07-26) because the directive's own closing step ('[O] commitea el spec
      ... cuando Stripe calibre') depended on an agent identity (Opus/[O]) that stopped being
      reliably available for BBH-adjacent work mid-arc (repeated AUP false-positive flags, see
      memory project_aup_false_positives). A parallel status query to C2 (bbh-wsl) about this
      same work independently answered wrong on 2 of 5 points (see the corrected report,
      TASKS.vsm session log 2026-07-26) — not fabrication, but an answer given without checking
      git log / the actual files first. The standard going forward, for every agent in this
      recursion including this one: verify against the live source (git log, ls, the file
      itself) before reporting status, the same discipline this project already applies to its
      own infra (R4/R5). A report is a claim until it cites primary evidence.",

  next: "(1) runtime_gate: build check_policy(tool, target) reading restrictions.json,
      block on prohibited_methods match — this is the highest-leverage open item, it is what
      turns a captured policy into an actual safety floor for a run. (2) corpus_expansion:
      spot-check gitlab/affirm/matomo/airtable extractions against their real pages before
      trusting them at Stripe's confidence level. (3) mining_pipeline: OpportunityScore is
      lower priority than (1) — it affects target SELECTION, not authorization; a wrong
      selection wastes effort, a missing runtime gate risks an out-of-scope action.
      (4) separately: back-port the 4-condition gate decision into finding_validation_gate.spec.vsm.",
}
